//*
# Generate the starter presentation

Generates a six-slide introduction to SPL, including the type builders.
Run it from the repository root. Generation uses an agent and writes presentation files;
`spl check generate-presentation.spl` checks the workflow without making model calls.

    spl run generate-presentation.spl
*//

---
model: gpt-6.1-terra
---

const slides = [
    `Semantic Prompt Language: natural-language instructions for models and agents, interleaved with
     TypeScript in one .spl file; show the three additions (Markdown comments, --- blocks, @name references);
     distinguish deterministic checks from probabilistic model output`,
    `Getting started ->
     1. installation from npm (Node.js 24.15 or newer)
     2. API-key login and setting up VS Code
     3. spl run lang/examples/basics.spl; spl run lang/examples/typed-data.spl without a model; spl check`,
    `Code and blocks -> code is TypeScript with the library already in scope and types erased by Node.js;
     explain the block header (mode, model, reasoning, outputVar, outputType), ask, agent and codegen modes,
     @name inputs and ->[Type] @name outputs that become ordinary variables;
     show a block inside an if or a loop and a compact exact-code example`,
    `Types -> the type builders: Enum, Struct, List, Union, Nullable, Typedef and class types with methods;
     show Typedef('Money', Int) with integer-cent arithmetic and an ask block with outputType: Invoice;
     coerce converts what a model sends, parse validates strictly;
     annotations are model advice, assertions check business rules`,
    `Append-only traces and human input -> record a run with --trace run.jsonl;
     human input in the terminal or via repeated --human flags;
     reuse the same --trace path to resume or replay deterministically, choose another file to restart`,
    `Restrictions and MCP -> enforce and forbid are prompt guidance, restrict is runtime enforcement,
     in code and as block header keys; show filesystem, command and MCP tool restrictions;
     restrictions cover library tools and agents, not Node.js APIs called directly, and are not an OS sandbox`,
];

const outline = slides.map((slide, index) => `Slide ${index + 1} - ${slide}`).join('\n\n');

---
mode: agent
enforce: Use modern-web-standards skill
forbid: Hallucinating

Read the current README, the docs-template guides and the runnable examples before writing.
Create a beautiful presentation of this repo for new starters: exactly 6 slides in HTML
and a matching 6-page PDF. Use valid SPL examples and explain implemented features only.
Follow the outline in @outline and save the files to the folder presentations.
---
